-		// The grant stamps the new holder's class: from this instant
-		// Interrupt may close this ticket's socket once the dialer files it.
+		// The grant stamps the new holder's class and drops the old holder's
+		// filed socket: from the grant until the new dialer files its own via
+		// noteConn the lane owns no connection, so Interrupt closes nothing and
+		// noteConn accepts the fresh socket. Leaving the previous holder's (now
+		// closed) conn filed here made noteConn reject the next dial's live
+		// socket and close it — a background plane died as a spurious transport
+		// error, and the read-ahead pass lost a plane it had parked to resume
+		// (B3 flake, 2026-11-20).
 		st.bg = w.class == ClassBackground
+		st.conn = nil
 		w.granted = true
 		close(w.ready)
 		return
